--- Rosetta Code: Erdős-Nicolas numbers
--- https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Erd%C5%91s-Nicolas_numbers
--- A divisor sieve: each d from 2 up is added to the running sum of every
--- multiple of it, so a number's sum grows through its divisors in ascending
--- order. A number whose sum equals it before its next proper divisor is added
--- is an Erdős–Nicolas number (a perfect number reaches its own sum only with
--- its last proper divisor). The search runs to two million, past the eighth;
--- the ninth, 61,900,800, would need a sieve thirty times as long.

--- each Erdős–Nicolas number up to `limit`, keyed to how many of its first
--- divisors sum to it
fn erdos_nicolas[limit]
    total = for n in range[limit + 1]
        1
    count = total
    found = map[]
    d = 2
    while d + d lte limit
        n = d + d
        while n lte limit
            if total[n] eq n
                found = set[found, n, count[n]]
            total[n] = total[n] + d
            count[n] = count[n] + 1
            n = n + d
        d = d + 1
    return found

found = erdos_nicolas[2000000]
for n in keys[found]
    log['`fmt[n, width = 9]` equals the sum of its first `found[n]` divisors']
